    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0723" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1415: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Officer in Charge at New Delhi</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Merrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-09T11:00:00+05:30">August 9, 1942—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 9—6:03 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>581. Gandhi,<anchor n="31" xml:id="d599-f1"/> Nehru,<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d599-f2"/> Azad,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d599-f3"/> and about 20 other
                    Congress leaders were arrested early this morning (reference my 580, August 8, 7
                        p.m.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d599-f4"/>).</p>
                <p>Speaking before All India Congress Committee last night Gandhi stated that he
                    would make every effort to see Viceroy<anchor n="35" xml:id="d599-f5"/> before
                    launching struggle but Government was apparently unimpressed by this
                    statement.</p>
                <p>There is as yet no news as to whether, in view of foregoing, movement will be
                    started forthwith.</p>
                <pb facs="0724" n="712" xml:id="pg712"/>
                <p>The Indian defense member confirmed to me last night the explanation given in the
                    last paragraph of telegram referred to above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Merrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d599-f1" n="31" xml:id="d599-f1-content">
                <p>Mohandas K. Gandhi, leader of civil disobedience movement in India.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d599-f2" n="32" xml:id="d599-f2-content">
                <p>Pandit Jawaharlal Nehru, Congress Party leader; associated with Gandhi in
                    opposition to British rule in India.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d599-f3" n="33" xml:id="d599-f3-content">
                <p>Maulana Azad, President of the Congress Party.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d599-f4" n="34" xml:id="d599-f4-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg708">p. 708</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d599-f5" n="35" xml:id="d599-f5-content">
                <p>Marquess of Linlithgow.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
